From 1f4278e4cb9f97ccb7c71c19ac7cfa40f30f89af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: spotUP <retroranksmail@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:10:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 22/22] upkg: browse hands its script the three lists from one
 load

upkg browse used to skip loading the feeds and the status file, and the
browse script then ran upkg list, list-installed and list-upgradable:
three more loads of upkg, about 3 s each on a 68k from a PFS3 disk
(measured on a Replay, 2026-10-21). browse now loads them, writes the
three lists to <dir>upkg-lists.<pid>.{all,inst,upg} exactly as a pipe
gets them, names the prefix in UPKG_BROWSE_LISTS for the script and
removes the files when the script returns. dir is TMPDIR, else T:,
else /tmp, as the script picks its own temp file.

list-browse PREFIX writes the same three files, so the script reloads
the lists after an install or removal with one upkg run instead of
three.
